Chapter: CmacTest

  cites Foreword chapter Cmac

 AES-CMAC verified against the RFC 4493 test vectors (key 2b7e1516...):
 the empty message, one full block, and a 40-byte message exercise the
 K2/pad, K1, and K2/pad-with-chain paths respectively. Expected tags are
 the published RFC 4493 constants. opening returns the count of passing
 checks.

Section: Helpers

  bytes-eq : List Integer, List Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq (a) (b) =
   if list-length a /= list-length b then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b 0 (list-length a)

  bytes-eq-loop : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq-loop (a) (b) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then True
   else if list-at a i /= list-at b i then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b (i + 1) len

  flag : Boolean -> Integer
  flag (b) = if b then 1 else 0

Section: Vectors

  rfc-key : List Integer
  rfc-key = [43, 126, 21, 22, 40, 174, 210, 166, 171, 247, 21, 136, 9, 207, 79, 60]

  msg-16 : List Integer
  msg-16 = [107, 193, 190, 226, 46, 64, 159, 150, 233, 61, 126, 17, 115, 147, 23, 42]

  msg-40 : List Integer
  msg-40 = [107, 193, 190, 226, 46, 64, 159, 150, 233, 61, 126, 17, 115, 147, 23, 42, 174, 45, 138, 87, 30, 3, 172, 156, 158, 183, 111, 172, 69, 175, 142, 81, 48, 200, 28, 70, 163, 92, 228, 17]

Section: Checks

  check-empty : Integer
  check-empty =
   flag (bytes-eq (aes-cmac rfc-key []) [187, 29, 105, 41, 233, 89, 55, 40, 127, 163, 125, 18, 155, 117, 103, 70])

  check-16 : Integer
  check-16 =
   flag (bytes-eq (aes-cmac rfc-key msg-16) [7, 10, 22, 180, 107, 77, 65, 68, 247, 155, 221, 157, 208, 74, 40, 124])

  check-40 : Integer
  check-40 =
   flag (bytes-eq (aes-cmac rfc-key msg-40) [223, 166, 103, 71, 222, 154, 230, 48, 48, 202, 50, 97, 20, 151, 200, 39])

  opening : Integer =
   let a = check-empty
   in let b = check-16
   in let c = check-40
   in a + b + c
